## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for a real multi-tenant data routing bug with data residency risk, ensuring traceability from detection to verification and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant IDs, and route metadata
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine with clear escalations
- Linked logs/traces in CAPA records for auditability
- Canary rollout and RCA templates with measurable metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST API skeleton for CAPA creation
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, tenantId, routeInfo } = req.body;
  // persist CAPA and link logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', status: 'open' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune thresholds across regions?
- What automated checks would prevent reintroduction of the misrouting in future deployments?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

